    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d954">

                <pb facs="0889" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.00/24.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d954-f1"
                        /></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>158. Your 145 of March 30, 1 p.m. There is no objection to your attending a
                    meeting of the Diplomatic Corps or of calling a meeting thereof at the instance
                    of some one other than yourself, provided your own attitude is
                    non-committal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d954-f1" n="1" xml:id="d954-f1-content">
                <p>The omitted part of this telegram refers to Claims, which see.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
